Subject: amd-pstate: tolerate unsupported per-policy boost

ARB33P BIOS 1.23 advertises CPB globally but rejects the policy11 boost
write with EINVAL. Keep other failures fatal while allowing the remaining
amd-pstate profile controls to apply. Remove this patch after First ARPC
provides a firmware fix.

Upstream context:
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/upower/power-profiles-daemon/-/issues/189
---
diff --git a/src/ppd-driver-amd-pstate.c b/src/ppd-driver-amd-pstate.c
index cc9be85..5a9ba7b 100644
--- a/src/ppd-driver-amd-pstate.c
+++ b/src/ppd-driver-amd-pstate.c
@@ -222 +222,2 @@ apply_pref_to_devices (GPtrArray   *devices,
     g_autofree char *min_freq_path = NULL;
+    g_autoptr(GError) boost_error = NULL;
@@ -240,2 +241,10 @@ apply_pref_to_devices (GPtrArray   *devices,
-      if (!ppd_utils_write (cpb, cpb_pref, error))
-        return FALSE;
+      if (!ppd_utils_write (cpb, cpb_pref, &boost_error)) {
+        if (!g_error_matches (boost_error,
+                              G_IO_ERROR,
+                              G_IO_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT)) {
+          g_propagate_error (error, g_steal_pointer (&boost_error));
+          return FALSE;
+        }
+
+        g_warning ("Ignoring unsupported boost control for %s", base);
+      }
